  "tag": "rp4g",
  "structural_change": "RP4e CTS gate (PVE1 smh_tile_rp4e-20261016-152829): in-flow post-CTS setup WNS -280 ps on 4,683 endpoints (u.g_gl[2].u_d3, clk_region[1]->[2]), hold -234 on 5,096; clk_region[0] avg sink wire 1272 um depth 10-11 vs clk_region[1] 0 leaf buffers; rp4d -391.7 on u_v2 ([0]->[1]). Cause = paths crossing the 10 soft CTS roots + 18 hard entries with different trees. Owner 2026-10-16 neighbour-relative clocking: one regional root per tile, no cross-root equalisation. rp4f: same rp4e floorplan/pins/children/RTL body/cycles; the 28 clock ports collapse to ONE port clk (W face y 651.996, centre band) and one TritonCTS root (macro clustering) instead of the rp4f spine; parallel variant. OT_SMH_RP4_SRST: all rp4 glue resets synchronous from the registered regional tree (rp4e hold -234 at RESETN removal fixed at the source, not by padding).",
  "purpose": "MATVEC body clock-structure closure only; not attention/fullSM/native chip qualification.",
